{{- /*
  Infisical agent template -> /opt/wishly/infra/.env  on the PVE VM.

  Sibling of env.mac.tmpl. They are deliberately separate files rather than one
  template with conditionals, because the two hosts genuinely differ in the one
  thing that matters: the Mac runs a Postgres container, this VM uses RDS.
  Keeping them apart makes that difference a one-line diff instead of branching
  logic you have to simulate in your head.

  Every secret the machine identity can read is rendered as KEY=value, so the
  Infisical secret NAMES must match the env var names the app expects. Adding a
  secret in the dashboard propagates here with no change to this file.

  DATABASE_URL is NOT a literal below. It carries the RDS password, so it comes
  from Infisical — and a literal would silently WIN over the Infisical value,
  because literals are rendered after the secret loop and Docker Compose takes
  the last duplicate key. That failure mode is invisible: the stack comes up
  pointed at the wrong database and looks perfectly healthy.
*/ -}}
# Rendered by the Infisical agent. DO NOT EDIT — changes are overwritten.
{{ with secret "8cbc2c7e-fa27-4e37-b3c9-15642fc8ca08" "dev" "/" }}
{{- range . }}
{{ .Key }}={{ .Value }}
{{- end }}
{{- end }}

# --- Non-secret configuration (literals; keep out of Infisical) -------------

# This VM is the dev deployment — the role the Mac used to hold. Production is a
# later step (DEPLOYMENT-PLAN T9), and it changes this line first.
ENVIRONMENT=dev

# Real Clerk verification is ON and stays on. `prod` would disable the bypass
# permanently regardless; at `dev` this line is what keeps it off.
AUTH_DEV_BYPASS=false

# REQUIRED. Without it the API cannot fetch JWKS and every authenticated request
# 401s while the app otherwise looks perfectly healthy.
CLERK_FRONTEND_API=https://clerk.wishly.dev
EMAIL_FROM=reminders@wishly.dev

# The SPA is served from wishly.dev (Cloudflare Pages); the API runs here behind
# the api-dev tunnel. Both origins must be listed or the SPA's calls fail CORS.
# No localhost entry: nothing serves a dev frontend from this VM.
APP_BASE_URL=https://wishly.dev
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://wishly.dev,https://www.wishly.dev

# From Infisical, and deliberately absent as literals here:
#   DATABASE_URL   — the RDS DSN, password included. Must carry ?sslmode=require:
#                    the parameter group sets rds.force_ssl=1, so a plain DSN is
#                    refused at connect time.
#   TUNNEL_TOKEN   — an empty literal would shadow it and cloudflared would come
#                    up with no tunnel.
#   PREFECT_API_URL / PREFECT_API_KEY — the Cloud workspace and its key.
#   CLERK_SECRET_KEY, CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET
#   RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET
